Crispy Doom needs a Doom IWAD
=============================

No game data comes with Crispy Doom. Copy an IWAD into this drawer (beside
the crispy-doom program), and Crispy Doom finds it by itself:

  doom1.wad      Doom shareware (Episode 1, free to download)
  doom.wad       The Ultimate Doom or registered Doom
  doom2.wad      Doom II
  tnt.wad, plutonia.wad   Final Doom
  freedoom1.wad, freedoom2.wad   Freedoom (free, https://freedoom.github.io)

Upper or lower case doesn't matter. Or start it from a Shell with -iwad and
the file's full name, for example:

  crispy-doom -iwad Work:WADs/DOOM2.WAD

An IWAD elsewhere is also found through SetEnv DOOMWADDIR (one directory)
or DOOMWADPATH (several, separated by ';').

PWADs: crispy-doom -file Work:WADs/mymap.wad (Shell), or an ARGS tool type
on the program's icon, e.g. ARGS=-file mymap.wad -warp 1

Configuration and saved games are written to the User drawer beside the
program (made on the first run); screenshots to the current
directory.
